  "body": "### Describe the feature you'd like to request\n\nBased on https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/2147#issuecomment-2692174445. Note that this is not the same feature request as the original request. This request does not concern disabling public access.\n\nI would like to have a user redirected if the user tries to access a board URL without being logged in. Note that for the redirect it is irrelevant if the board actually exists or if the user has access if the board exists.\n\nSo if a user is not logged in and accesses:\nhttps://homarr.example.com/ -> redirect to https://homarr.example.com/auth/login\nhttps://homarr.example.com/boards/aboardthatdoesexist -> redirect to https://homarr.example.com/auth/login\nhttps://homarr.example.com/boards/aboardthatdoesnotexist -> redirect to https://homarr.example.com/auth/login\n\nOr logically:\n1. A user not logged in attempts to access a board URL. It does not matter at this stage if the board exists or not, or if the user has access to an existing board.\n\n2. **Not-logged-in user is redirected to login page.**\n\n3. User logs in (ideally configured for automatic login, such as with OIDC).\n\n4. **Logged-in user is redirected back to the board URL that was originally requested.**\n\n5. Now Homarr evaluates if the board exists and if the user has access.\n\nSteps 2 and 4 concern this feature request.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_",
